-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), regulations 50, 51 and 51.1: EMPLOYMENT MEASURES, the
-- WORK-FORCE REDUCTION PROCESS, and the PRESCRIBED CIRCUMSTANCES for subparagraph 29(c)(xiv) of the Act.
-- Written by the piece agent er3 (Sonnet 5.5) on 2026-10-24 from the unofficial plain-text rendering
-- SOR-96-332.txt; nothing here is claimed to be verified against the official text.
--
-- Out of range: s 25(1)(b)(i) (the measures a claimant may be referred to, piece ei2), ss 59(b) and 63 (employment
-- support measures and agreements, ei2), s 29(c) and 30 (just cause for leaving an employment and the
-- disqualification for leaving without it, ei2). Each is an input.
-- Reg 51.1 sends the reader to the list of immediate family of reg 55(2), which is er3-outside-canada's.

§ `Regulation 50 -- employment measures`

-- (a) An employment support measure referred to in paragraph 59(b) of the Act, established to (i) help insured
-- participants start businesses or become self-employed, or (ii) provide insured participants with employment
-- opportunities through which they can gain work experience to improve their long-term employment prospects.
-- src:761 | (a) an employment support measure referred to in paragraph 59(b) of the Act that is established to
-- src:762 | (i) help insured participants start businesses or become self-employed, or
-- src:763 | (ii) provide insured participants with employment opportunities through which they can gain work experience to improve their long-term employment prospects; and
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 50(a) (src:761-763)
GIVEN `the measure is an employment support measure referred to in paragraph 59(b) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is established to help insured participants start businesses or become self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is established to provide insured participants with employment opportunities through which they can gain work experience to improve their long-term employment prospects` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 50(a) an employment support measure referred to in paragraph 59(b) of the Act that is prescribed` IF
        `the measure is an employment support measure referred to in paragraph 59(b) of the Act`
    AND (   `it is established to help insured participants start businesses or become self-employed`
         OR `it is established to provide insured participants with employment opportunities through which they can gain work experience to improve their long-term employment prospects`)

-- (b) A measure that is the subject of an agreement under section 63 of the Act, established for the same two ends.
-- src:764 | (b) a measure that is the subject of an agreement under section 63 of the Act that is established to
-- src:765 | (i) help insured participants start businesses or become self-employed, or
-- src:766 | (ii) provide insured participants with employment opportunities through which they can gain work experience to improve their long-term employment prospects.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 50(b) (src:764-766)
GIVEN `the measure is the subject of an agreement under section 63 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is established to help insured participants start businesses or become self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is established to provide insured participants with employment opportunities through which they can gain work experience to improve their long-term employment prospects` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 50(b) a measure that is the subject of an agreement under section 63 of the Act that is prescribed` IF
        `the measure is the subject of an agreement under section 63 of the Act`
    AND (   `it is established to help insured participants start businesses or become self-employed`
         OR `it is established to provide insured participants with employment opportunities through which they can gain work experience to improve their long-term employment prospects`)

-- src:760 | 50 The following are prescribed for the purposes of subparagraph 25(1)(b)(i) of the Act:
-- src:761 | (a) an employment support measure referred to in paragraph 59(b) of the Act that is established to
-- src:762 | (i) help insured participants start businesses or become self-employed, or
-- src:763 | (ii) provide insured participants with employment opportunities through which they can gain work experience to improve their long-term employment prospects; and
-- src:764 | (b) a measure that is the subject of an agreement under section 63 of the Act that is established to
-- src:765 | (i) help insured participants start businesses or become self-employed, or
-- src:766 | (ii) provide insured participants with employment opportunities through which they can gain work experience to improve their long-term employment prospects.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 50 (src:760-766)
GIVEN `the measure is an employment support measure referred to in paragraph 59(b) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the measure is the subject of an agreement under section 63 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is established to help insured participants start businesses or become self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is established to provide insured participants with employment opportunities through which they can gain work experience to improve their long-term employment prospects` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 50 the measure is prescribed for the purposes of subparagraph 25(1)(b)(i) of the Act` IF
       `reg 50(a) an employment support measure referred to in paragraph 59(b) of the Act that is prescribed` `the measure is an employment support measure referred to in paragraph 59(b) of the Act` `it is established to help insured participants start businesses or become self-employed` `it is established to provide insured participants with employment opportunities through which they can gain work experience to improve their long-term employment prospects`
    OR `reg 50(b) a measure that is the subject of an agreement under section 63 of the Act that is prescribed` `the measure is the subject of an agreement under section 63 of the Act` `it is established to help insured participants start businesses or become self-employed` `it is established to provide insured participants with employment opportunities through which they can gain work experience to improve their long-term employment prospects`

§ `Regulation 51 -- work-force reduction process`

-- (2) An employer work-force reduction process is a process (a) initiated by the employer; (b) whose objective is a
-- permanent reduction in the overall number of employees; (c) that offers employees the option to leave employment
-- voluntarily; and (d) whose elements, including those of (a) to (c), are documented by the employer.
-- src:772 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), an employer work-force reduction process is a process
-- src:773 | (a) that is initiated by the employer;
-- src:774 | (b) that has as its objective a permanent reduction in the overall number of employees;
-- src:775 | (c) that offers employees the option to leave employment voluntarily; and
-- src:776 | (d) the elements of which, including the elements described in paragraphs (a) to (c), are documented by the employer.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 51(2) (src:772-776)
GIVEN `the process is initiated by the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its objective is a permanent reduction in the overall number of employees` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it offers employees the option to leave employment voluntarily` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its elements, including those described in paragraphs (a) to (c), are documented by the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 51(2) employer work-force reduction process` IF
        `the process is initiated by the employer`
    AND `its objective is a permanent reduction in the overall number of employees`
    AND `it offers employees the option to leave employment voluntarily`
    AND `its elements, including those described in paragraphs (a) to (c), are documented by the employer`

-- (1) Subject to the Act and the Regulations, but notwithstanding section 30 of the Act (the disqualification for
-- leaving without just cause), a claimant who has left employment in accordance with an employer work-force
-- reduction process that preserves the employment of co-workers may be paid benefits where (a) the claimant
-- accepted an offer to leave that employment voluntarily; and (b) the employer has confirmed that the claimant's
-- leaving resulted in the actual preservation of the employment of a co-worker whose employment would otherwise
-- have been terminated in the course of the process. "May be paid": the text lets benefits be paid, it does not
-- order it; the rule gives the conditions, not the Commission's decision.
-- src:769 | 51 (1) Subject to the Act and these Regulations, but notwithstanding section 30 of the Act, a claimant who has left employment in accordance with an employer work-force reduction process that preserves the employment of co-workers may be paid benefits where
-- src:770 | (a) the claimant accepted an offer to leave that employment voluntarily; and
-- src:771 | (b) the employer has confirmed that the claimant's leaving resulted in the actual preservation of the employment of a co-worker whose employment would otherwise have been terminated in the course of the work-force reduction process.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 51(1) (src:769-771)
GIVEN `the claimant left employment in accordance with an employer work-force reduction process` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the process is an employer work-force reduction process under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the process preserves the employment of co-workers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant accepted an offer to leave that employment voluntarily` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer has confirmed that the claimant's leaving resulted in the actual preservation of the employment of a co-worker whose employment would otherwise have been terminated in the course of the process` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 51(1) benefits may be paid notwithstanding section 30 of the Act to a claimant who left under a work-force reduction process` IF
        `the claimant left employment in accordance with an employer work-force reduction process`
    AND `the process is an employer work-force reduction process under subsection (2)`
    AND `the process preserves the employment of co-workers`
    AND `the claimant accepted an offer to leave that employment voluntarily`
    AND `the employer has confirmed that the claimant's leaving resulted in the actual preservation of the employment of a co-worker whose employment would otherwise have been terminated in the course of the process`

§ `Regulation 51.1 -- prescribed circumstances for subparagraph 29(c)(xiv) of the Act`

-- (a) An obligation to accompany to another residence a person with whom the claimant has been cohabiting in a
-- conjugal relationship for a period of less than one year, where (i) the claimant or that person has had a child
-- or adopted a child during that period, (ii) the claimant or that person is expecting the birth of a child, or
-- (iii) a child has been placed with the claimant or that person during that period for the purpose of adoption.
-- "A period of less than one year" is counted to the day the claimant left their employment.
-- src:780 | (a) circumstances in which a claimant has an obligation to accompany to another residence a person with whom the claimant has been cohabiting in a conjugal relationship for a period of less than one year and where
-- src:781 | (i) the claimant or that person has had a child during that period or has adopted a child during that period,
-- src:782 | (ii) the claimant or that person is expecting the birth of a child, or
-- src:783 | (iii) a child has been placed with the claimant or that person during that period for the purpose of adoption; and
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 51.1(a) (src:780-783)
GIVEN `the claimant has an obligation to accompany to another residence a person with whom the claimant has been cohabiting in a conjugal relationship` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first day of the cohabitation` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the claimant left their employment` IS A DATE
      `the claimant or that person has had a child during that period or has adopted a child during that period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant or that person is expecting the birth of a child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a child has been placed with the claimant or that person during that period for the purpose of adoption` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 51.1(a) an obligation to accompany a partner of less than one year to another residence` IF
        `the claimant has an obligation to accompany to another residence a person with whom the claimant has been cohabiting in a conjugal relationship`
    AND (`the day on which the claimant left their employment` LESS THAN (`add years` `the first day of the cohabitation` 1))
    AND (   `the claimant or that person has had a child during that period or has adopted a child during that period`
         OR `the claimant or that person is expecting the birth of a child`
         OR `a child has been placed with the claimant or that person during that period for the purpose of adoption`)

-- (b) An obligation to care for a member of the claimant's immediate family within the meaning of subsection 55(2).
-- src:784 | (b) circumstances in which a claimant has an obligation to care for a member of their immediate family within the meaning of subsection 55(2).
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 51.1(b) (src:784)
GIVEN `the claimant has an obligation to care for the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      relationship IS A `er3 Relationship of a person to the claimant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 51.1(b) an obligation to care for a member of the immediate family` IF
        `the claimant has an obligation to care for the person`
    AND `reg 55(2) a member of the claimant's immediate family` relationship

-- "other reasonable circumstances include" (a) and (b): an open list. The two circumstances are reasonable
-- circumstances for the purposes of s 29(c)(xiv); anything else is not decided here, so the answer is JUST TRUE for
-- a listed circumstance and NOTHING for anything else, never FALSE.
-- src:779 | 51.1 For the purposes of subparagraph 29(c)(xiv) of the Act, other reasonable circumstances include
-- src:780 | (a) circumstances in which a claimant has an obligation to accompany to another residence a person with whom the claimant has been cohabiting in a conjugal relationship for a period of less than one year and where
-- src:781 | (i) the claimant or that person has had a child during that period or has adopted a child during that period,
-- src:782 | (ii) the claimant or that person is expecting the birth of a child, or
-- src:783 | (iii) a child has been placed with the claimant or that person during that period for the purpose of adoption; and
-- src:784 | (b) circumstances in which a claimant has an obligation to care for a member of their immediate family within the meaning of subsection 55(2).
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 51.1 (src:779-784)
GIVEN `the circumstance is the one described in paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the circumstance is the one described in paragraph (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 51.1 other reasonable circumstances include the circumstance` IS
    IF `the circumstance is the one described in paragraph (a)` OR `the circumstance is the one described in paragraph (b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
